3.1 Global API Standards
text
BASE URL:       https://api.adtowns.com/api/v1
CONTENT-TYPE:   application/json
AUTH HEADER:    Authorization: Bearer {jwt_token}
 
STANDARD RESPONSE ENVELOPE:
{
  "success": true,
  "data": { ... },
  "message": "Operation successful",
  "errors": null,
  "timestamp": "2025-05-12T10:30:00Z",
  "traceId": "abc123"
}
 
ERROR RESPONSE:
{
  "success": false,
  "data": null,
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "errors": [
    { "field": "PhoneNumber", "message": "Invalid format" }
  ],
  "timestamp": "2025-05-12T10:30:00Z",
  "traceId": "abc123"
}
 
HTTP STATUS CODES:
  200 OK              - Success
  201 Created         - Resource created
  400 Bad Request     - Validation error
  401 Unauthorized    - Missing/invalid token
  403 Forbidden       - Insufficient permissions
  404 Not Found       - Resource not found
  409 Conflict        - Concurrent conflict (pixel locked)
  429 Too Many Req    - Rate limit exceeded
  500 Internal Error  - Server error
3.2 AUTH API
text
POST   /api/v1/auth/otp/send
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Purpose:  Send OTP to phone number for login or registration
Auth:     None
Rate:     3 requests per phone per 10 minutes
 
REQUEST:
{
  "phoneNumber": "+919876543210",
  "purpose": "Login"  // Login | Register
}
 
RESPONSE 200:
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "otpSent": true,
    "expiresInSeconds": 300,
    "maskedPhone": "+91 XXXXXX3210"
  }
}
 
BUSINESS LOGIC:
  1. Validate phone format (Indian 10-digit)
  2. Check rate limit in Redis (key: otp:{phone})
  3. Generate 6-digit OTP
  4. Hash OTP with SHA256
  5. Store in OtpRequests table (expires in 5 minutes)
  6. Send via WhatsApp/SMS API
  7. Increment rate limit counter in Redis
 
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 
POST   /api/v1/auth/otp/verify
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Purpose:  Verify OTP and return JWT + Refresh Token
Auth:     None
 
REQUEST:
{
  "phoneNumber": "+919876543210",
  "otpCode": "482910",
  "purpose": "Login"
}
 
RESPONSE 200:
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "accessToken": "eyJ...",
    "refreshToken": "rft_...",
    "expiresIn": 3600,
    "seller": {
      "sellerId": 1,
      "businessName": "Ravi's Pizza",
      "isNewUser": false,
      "onboardingComplete": true
    }
  }
}
 
RESPONSE 400 (wrong OTP):
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Invalid OTP. 2 attempts remaining."
}
 
BUSINESS LOGIC:
  1. Find latest unused OTP for phone
  2. Check not expired
  3. Check attempt count < 5
  4. Compare hash
  5. If match: mark OTP used, generate JWT (1hr) + Refresh (30d)
  6. Store refresh token hash in DB
  7. Update LastLoginAt
 
